  "problem": "If $X={1,3,5,7}$ and $Y={1,2,3,4},$ then $X-Y=$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $X-Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the elements $1,3\\in Y$ are also in $X,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X-Y & ={1,3,5,7}-{1,2,3,4} \\\\  & ={5,7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
